{
  "conversation_lines": [
    {
      "turn_number": 1,
      "time": "2140-04-13 20:15:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Hi, I’m Dr. Lee. I’ll be taking care of you tonight. Can you tell me what happened before you came in?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 2,
      "time": "2140-04-13 20:16:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Hi, Doctor. I was at home yesterday afternoon and started feeling really lightheaded, like I was going to pass out. I called my neighbor, and when I woke up, I was on the floor."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 3,
      "time": "2140-04-13 20:17:45",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "How long do you think you were unconscious?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 4,
      "time": "2140-04-13 20:18:10",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’m not sure—maybe a few minutes? I remember calling my neighbor, then nothing until she found me."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 5,
      "time": "2140-04-13 20:19:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Okay. Any chest pain, shortness of breath, or palpitations before it happened?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 6,
      "time": "2140-04-13 20:19:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "No, nothing like that. Just the dizziness. And I’ve been feeling kind of off balance since—like I’m drunk when I walk."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 7,
      "time": "2140-04-13 20:20:15",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "I see. Any nausea, vision changes, or weakness?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 8,
      "time": "2140-04-13 20:20:45",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "No, but I do have a headache on the left side. Not the worst I’ve ever had, but it’s there."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 9,
      "time": "2140-04-13 20:21:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Got it. You mentioned poor appetite—did you eat much the day before?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 10,
      "time": "2140-04-13 20:22:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Not really. I wasn’t feeling well, so I didn’t eat much. But I did take my glyburide that morning."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 11,
      "time": "2140-04-13 20:22:45",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Even though you hadn’t eaten?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 12,
      "time": "2140-04-13 20:23:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes. But it didn’t feel like my usual low blood sugar—no shaking or sweating."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 13,
      "time": "2140-04-13 20:23:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That’s important. We’ll check your glucose and keep an eye on that. We also did an EKG, and it showed some changes in the heart tracing, but your cardiac enzymes were normal, so it’s unlikely a heart attack."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 14,
      "time": "2140-04-13 20:24:15",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Oh. Should I be worried about my heart?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 15,
      "time": "2140-04-13 20:24:45",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Not at this point. The changes could be due to your high blood pressure or other factors. We’re monitoring you on telemetry, and no arrhythmias have shown up."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 16,
      "time": "2140-04-14 08:30:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good morning. We did a CT scan of your head last night—no bleeding or stroke. But because of your balance issues, neurology recommended an MRI and MRA, which we did this morning."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 17,
      "time": "2140-04-14 08:31:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And what did they show?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 18,
      "time": "2140-04-14 08:32:15",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "No acute stroke or tumor. But there are signs of small vessel disease in the brain, which is common with high blood pressure and diabetes. Also, there’s mild narrowing at the start of the right vertebral artery, but it’s not severe."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 19,
      "time": "2140-04-14 08:33:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Could that be why I fell?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 20,
      "time": "2140-04-14 08:34:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Possibly, but the neurology team doesn’t think it caused a stroke. Given your recent cold symptoms—cough, congestion—the leading thought is labyrinthitis, an inner ear issue that affects balance."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 21,
      "time": "2140-04-14 08:35:15",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Oh, I didn’t think of that. I’ve had a stuffy nose for a few days."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 22,
      "time": "2140-04-14 08:36:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That fits. Labyrinthitis can cause dizziness, imbalance, and even a brief loss of consciousness in some cases."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 23,
      "time": "2140-04-14 14:20:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We got your urine test results back. It showed cocaine use."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 24,
      "time": "2140-04-14 14:21:15",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I… I haven’t used it recently. Maybe a few weeks ago. I know it’s not good, but I’m trying to stop."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 25,
      "time": "2140-04-14 14:22:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "I appreciate your honesty. Cocaine can cause serious heart issues, especially with high blood pressure. It can also trigger arrhythmias or worsen artery narrowing."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 26,
      "time": "2140-04-14 14:23:45",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That’s scary. I didn’t know it could affect my heart like that."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 27,
      "time": "2140-04-14 14:24:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "It can. Because of this, we’re stopping your propranolol. Combining it with cocaine can increase the risk of severe high blood pressure or heart complications."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 28,
      "time": "2140-04-14 14:25:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "But I take that for my headaches. Will I get more of them now?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 29,
      "time": "2140-04-14 14:26:45",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ll keep you on topiramate and acetazolamide, which also help with migraines and pseudotumor. We’ll discuss long-term options with your neurologist."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 30,
      "time": "2140-04-14 14:27:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay, that makes sense."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 31,
      "time": "2140-04-14 16:10:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Your blood pressure was high when you came in—172 over 100. We restarted your enalapril and amlodipine, and it’s now well-controlled."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 32,
      "time": "2140-04-14 16:11:15",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Good. I’ve been skipping my BP meds sometimes when I feel fine."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 33,
      "time": "2140-04-14 16:12:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "I understand, but with your history, it’s important to take them daily. High blood pressure increases stroke and heart risks, especially with your other conditions."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 34,
      "time": "2140-04-14 16:13:15",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’ll do better. I promise."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 35,
      "time": "2140-04-15 09:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good news—we’re discharging you today. Your labs are stable, imaging shows no acute issues, and your balance is a bit better."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 36,
      "time": "2140-04-15 09:01:15",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That’s great. But I’m still a little wobbly. Is that normal?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 37,
      "time": "2140-04-15 09:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, it can take time to recover from labyrinthitis. A physical therapist will come to your home for gait and balance training."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 38,
      "time": "2140-04-15 09:03:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay, that helps. What about my medications?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 39,
      "time": "2140-04-15 09:04:15",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’ll go home with your usual meds except propranolol—we’re stopping that permanently due to the cocaine use. All others are adjusted slightly, and instructions are in your discharge papers."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 40,
      "time": "2140-04-15 09:05:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And I should stop using cocaine for good?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 41,
      "time": "2140-04-15 09:06:15",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Absolutely. It’s dangerous for your heart and brain. Please consider speaking with a counselor or support group—we can help connect you."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 42,
      "time": "2140-04-15 09:07:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I will. Thank you, Doctor. I really appreciate your help."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 43,
      "time": "2140-04-15 09:07:45",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re welcome. Take care, and keep those follow-up appointments."
    }
  ],
  "summary": {
    "admission_start": "2140-04-13 19:54:00",
    "admission_end": "2140-04-15 16:34:00",
    "summary_paragraph": "A woman with a history of hypertension, type 2 diabetes, chronic migraines, pseudotumor cerebri, and other comorbidities was admitted after an episode of syncope followed by persistent lightheadedness and gait instability. She had poor oral intake and took glyburide without eating, raising concern for hypoglycemia, though she lacked typical symptoms. Initial evaluation showed new EKG changes but negative cardiac enzymes. MRI/MRA revealed no acute stroke but mild stenosis of the right vertebral artery and small vessel ischemic disease. Given recent URI symptoms and clinical findings, labyrinthitis was diagnosed as the likely cause of her vertigo and ataxia. A urine toxicology screen was positive for cocaine, leading to discontinuation of propranolol due to cardiovascular risks. Her blood pressure and glucose were managed during admission, and she was discharged home with a walker, home physical therapy, and updated medications, including permanent discontinuation of propranolol and counseling to cease cocaine use.",
    "problems": [
      "Labyrinthitis, unspecified",
      "Syncope and collapse",
      "Lack of coordination",
      "Unspecified essential hypertension",
      "Dysmetabolic syndrome X",
      "Benign intracranial hypertension",
      "Hypopotassemia",
      "Cocaine abuse, unspecified",
      "Migraine, unspecified, without mention of intractable migraine without mention of status migrainosus",
      "Anxiety state, unspecified",
      "Depressive disorder, not elsewhere classified",
      "Diabetes with neurological manifestations, type II or unspecified type, not stated as uncontrolled",
      "Gastroparesis",
      "Other chronic pulmonary heart diseases",
      "Other diseases of vocal cords"
    ]
  }
}
